  "findings": [
    {
      "text": "Instruction-finetuned Flan models produce toxic [RealToxicityPrompts](/evals/real-toxicity-prompts) continuations less often than PaLM at all scales for both toxic and non-toxic prompts.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "27",
        "pdfPage": 27,
        "quote": "In Table 6, we observe that the probability of instruction finetuned Flan models to produce toxic continuations\nis lower at all scales, and that this effect holds for both sets of input prompts."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Flan-T5-XXL can show higher continuation toxicity than Flan-PaLM and even the human baseline at high prompt toxicity.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "27",
        "pdfPage": 27,
        "quote": "Flan-T5-XXL seems to perform\ndifferently than Flan-PaLM models at higher prompt toxicity, even producing TPC worse the human baselines"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Identity-term prompts show reduced toxic continuations after Flan, but high tail toxicity and identity-group disparities remain.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "28",
        "pdfPage": 28,
        "quote": "Even though there is an overall reduction in toxicity across all the groups, the tail toxicity is still\nconsistently high."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "[Translation misgendering](/evals/google-translation-misgendering) impact of instruction finetuning on PaLM is mixed; all models do worse on correct \"she\" than \"he\" pronouns.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "32",
        "pdfPage": 32,
        "quote": "The impact of instruction finetuning on PaLM models is mixed, with no clear impact. All models\nperform worse on examples where the correct translation in English should include \"she\" pronouns rather"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Flan-T5 training data was not filtered for explicit content or assessed for existing biases.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "52",
        "pdfPage": 52,
        "quote": "Flan-T5 is fine-tuned on a large corpus of text data that was not filtered for explicit content or assessed"
      }
    }
  ],
